From 462ea067cd66ee4b97ed2f65b30ad76a7377e7f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 12:08:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Battle Style: apply to solo boots too

The generator was wired only into the netplay host path, so a solo boot never
wrote the code block at all -- the first field test picked a model and a venue
solo, got a stock battle, and reasonably concluded the feature was broken. The
codes were fine; they were never in the file.

Both launchers' solo boot buttons now run the same PrepareForStart the host
path uses. Cleanup for a solo session rides the core state: when emulation
reaches Uninitialized outside a netplay session, the session is over by
definition, so the block is stripped and a forced cheats flag handed back.
The hook stands down while a room is open -- in netplay the game stopping
does not mean the session ended, and the room-closed path owns cleanup there.

Also verified since the last build, by reading a clean main.dol directly: the
VS-mode BGM table at 0x802EAF0C is real -- three identical u32 slots holding
0x4F3, stm_bgm_tool_minnade, the multiplayer BGM family -- so the music
writes' address, width and semantics are confirmed against the game binary.

Version 1.2.1.
